s are not derivable from the line alone\n389\t * and are recovered from the preserved event: the session id lives in\n390\t * `producer.session_id`, and the `baseTime` fallback (used only when the line\n391\t * carries no timestamp of its own) is the preserved event's `occurred_at` —\n392\t * which is exactly the value the preservation path computed via\n393\t * `sessionBaseTime`, i.e. what a live capture of the same rollout file would\n394\t * compute too. The agent context is a third: it came from `session_meta` /\n395\t * `turn_context` lines that are not in `raw.data` at all, so it is read back\n396\t * off the preserved event's own `producer` — where the capture that preserved\n397\t * the line already recorded it. `reasoning` payloads are never preserved as `unrecognized` in\n398\t * the first place (they get their own `reasoning`-kind event instead), so\n399\t * this path never reconstructs provider-withheld content into a visible\n400\t * `conversation_turn`. Returns null when still uninterpretable.\n401\t */\n402\texport function renormalizeUnrecognized(\n403\t  event: EvidenceEvent,\n404\t  identity: GitUserIdentity,\n405\t): EventDraft | null {\n406\t  if (!event.raw || event.conversation === undefined) return null;\n407\t  const line = event.raw.data as CodexRolloutLine;\n408\t  const sessionId = event.producer.session_id ?? \"\";\n409\t  const agent: CodexAgentState = {};\n410\t  if (event.producer.source_version) agent.source_version = event.producer.source_version;\n411\t  if (event.producer.model) agent.model = event.producer.model;\n412\t  if (event.producer.provider) agent.provider = event.producer.provider;\n413\t  return convertLine(\n414\t    line,\n415\t    event.conversation.seq,\n416\t    sessionId,\n417\t    event.occurred_at,\n418\t    packageVersion(),\n419\t    identity,\n420\t    agent,\n421\t  );\n422\t}\n423\t\n424\texport async function runCodexHook(stdinJson: string): Promise<void> {\n425\t  try {\n426\t    const payload = JSON.parse