the 64KB stdout truncation bug\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6\n  modified: 2026-08-02T17:18:30.050Z\n---\n\n`src/adapters/opencode.ts` shipped in 0.17.0 on branch `worktree-opencode-adapter`, PR #2 (draft, unmerged as of 2026-08-02). Decisions the user approved, and the non-obvious findings behind them:\n\n- **Reads via `opencode export --pure <id>`, not the SQLite DB.** cledger has zero runtime deps and Node >= 20 (`node:sqlite` needs >= 22.5); opencode's schema is mid-migration (empty `session_message` beside populated `message`/`part`); and the DB also stores `credential.value` / `account.access_token`. `--sanitize` deliberately unused — cledger does its own redaction.\n- **`opencode export` truncates a piped stdout at ~64KB** (upstream Bun flush bug) and the truncated JSON can still parse — so it would silently capture partial conversations. Workaround: spawn with stdout on a temp-file fd. Verified 65516 bytes piped vs 446703 to a file. Not yet reported upstream.\n- **One event per *part*, not per message** — opencode's store is mutable and messages accumulate parts, so a part is the finest unit that stops changing. Unsettled (`running`) tool parts are skipped and hold the cursor back.\n- **`reasoning` parts are plaintext**, unlike Codex's encrypted ones, so they become visible `thinking` blocks — not the opaque `reasoning` kind (see [[project-cledger-reasoning-preservation]]).\n- **Trigger is a plugin, not a shell hook**: `cledger install opencode` writes `~/.config/opencode/plugin/cledger.js` listening for `session.idle`. Both `~/.config/opencode/plugin/` and project-local `.opencode/plugin/` auto-load a bare `export const server` — verified empirically. The child is spawned detached with stderr discarded so it can't block or garble the TUI.\n- The plugin reads the session id defensively across several key names; opencode's `Event` union isn't in the installed SDK typings and a live `session.idle` capture couldn't be completed (the probe run hung on the model call). Falls back to the most-recently-updated session for the directory.\n\nTwo limitations are on the README roadmap rather than fixed: `conversation.seq` is positional over a mutable store, so a `session revert` can shift positions and duplicate later parts; and **subagent sessions are skipped by every adapter** — the user explicitly asked for that as a future cross-adapter task, needing a schema relation (`spawned_by` link or `conversation.parent`) plus a `cledger log` display decision before turning claude-code, codex and opencode on together.\n\nRelated: [[project-ledger-ecosystem]] — turnbridge already had an opencode *target* (`src/targets/opencode.ts`) that writes sessions in via `opencode import`; this adapter is the read direction.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-opencode-adapter.md","memdirStamped":true,"originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"3dae3d53-657e-428b-b6af-5dcdd96cebf2","version":"2.1.220"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-02T17:18:57.183Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter/src/adapters/opencode.ts (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_018tpLnwwncudqu5qUmK78zD","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","head":"5476c74237583d41f5acff542b07f3b2eb42daf0","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","seq":268},"id":"ev1-7efdef9162c0be14bb24fc3384530f7856464045b41b68c666356e4825908bd3","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-02T17:11:47.482Z","producer":{"session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter/src/adapters/opencode.ts (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_018tpLnwwncudqu5qUmK78zD","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"699b0a17-599e-4647-ace1-dd2565d1e213","promptId":"7634b6a4-030c-450a-a53a-dc3f3ed5dda3","sessionId":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"699b0a17-599e-4647-ace1-dd2565d1e213","timestamp":"2026-08-02T17:11:47.482Z","toolUseResult":{"content":"/**\n * opencode adapter.\n *\n * Unlike claude-code and codex, opencode has no append-only transcript file:\n * sessions live in a mutable SQLite database at\n * `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. Rather than read that database, this\n * adapter shells out to opencode's own `opencode export <sessionID>`, which\n * emits `{info, messages: [{info, parts}]}` JSON. Three reasons:\n *\n *  1. cledger ships with no runtime dependencies and supports Node >= 20;\n *     `node:sqlite` would force both to change.\n *  2. opencode's schema is visibly mid-migration (an empty `session_message`\n *     table sits alongside the populated `message`/`part` tables it is\n *     evidently meant to replace). The export shape is the interface opencode\n *     documents; the tables are not.\n *  3. The same database holds `credential.value` and `account.access_token`.\n *     Reading conversations should not require opening the file that stores\n *     the user's API tokens.\n *\n * `--sanitize` is deliberately *not* passed to the export: cledger has its\n * own redaction stack, and letting opencode rewrite content would make event\n * ids depend on opencode's version.\n */\nimport { spawn } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { mkdir, mkdtemp, open, readFile, rm, writeFile } from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { findRepo, gitUserIdentity, type GitUserIdentity, type RepoInfo } from \"../git.js\";\nimport { appendEvents } from \"../store.js\";\nimport type { Actor, EventDraft, EvidenceEvent, ProducerAgentContext } from \"../schema.js\";\nimport {\n  countUnrecognized,\n  unrecognizedDraft,\n  warnUnrecognized,\n  type CaptureResult,\n} from \"./drift.js\";\n\nconst RAW_FORMAT = \"opencode-export-json/1\";\n\n/**\n * Part types carrying visible conversation content.\n *\n * `reasoning` belongs here, and that is a real difference from codex: codex's\n * reasoning items are provider-encrypted (`encrypted_content`) and can only\n * ever be preserved opaquely as `reasoning`-kind events, whereas opencode\n * stores reasoning as plain `text`. So it converts to an ordinary\n * `thinking` block inside a `conversation_turn`, exactly as claude-code's\n * thinking blocks do — no opacity marker, nothing withheld.\n */\nconst CONVERTIBLE_PART_TYPES = new Set([\"text\", \"reasoning\", \"tool\"]);\n\n/**\n * Part types deliberately not captured: per-step bookkeeping (`step-start` /\n * `step-finish` carry token counts and finish reasons, not content) and\n * `patch`, which is a content hash plus file list pointing into opencode's\n * private snapshot store — meaningless outside opencode, and the diff it\n * refers to is already in git.\n *\n * Kept deliberately short. opencode's binary also references `file`, `agent`,\n * `snapshot` and `todo` part types that no session on hand exercises; listing\n * them here on speculation would silently discard content on the first\n * session that used one. Leaving them out routes them through the drift path\n * instead — preserved raw-only, warned about, and upgradeable later by\n * `cledger renormalize`, which is exactly what that machinery is for.\n */\nconst KNOWN_SKIPPED_PART_TYPES = new Set([\"step-start\", \"step-finish\", \"patch\"]);\n\n/**\n * Tool-call states that will never change again. A `pending`/`running` part\n * is still being written; capturing it would bake a half-finished tool call\n * into an immutable event id. The capture loop skips unsettled parts *and*\n * holds the cursor back at the first one, so the finished version is picked\n * up on the next capture rather than being skipped forever.\n */\nconst SETTLED_TOOL_STATUSES = new Set([\"completed\", \"error\"]);\n\n/** Payload the installed opencode plugin sends on stdin (see install.ts). */\ninterface OpencodeHookPayload {\n  session_id?: string;\n  cwd?: string;\n  hook_event_name?: string;\n}\n\ninterface OpencodeSessionInfo {\n  id?: string;\n  /** Set on subagent sessions; those are skipped (see captureOpencodeExport). */\n  parentID?: string;\n  directory?: string;\n  title?: string;\n  /** opencode's own CLI version, e.g. \"1.18.5\". */\n  version?: string;\n  time?: { created?: number; updated?: number };\n}\n\ninterface OpencodeMessageInfo {\n  id?: string;\n  sessionID?: string;\n  role?: string;\n  /** Agent persona, e.g. \"build\" / \"plan\". */\n  agent?: string;\n  mode?: string;\n  /** Assistant messages state the model flat; user messages nest it. */\n  modelID?: string;\n  providerID?: string;\n  model?: { modelID?: string; providerID?: string };\n  time?: { created?: number; completed?: number };\n}\n\ninterface OpencodePart {\n  id?: string;\n  type?: string;\n  messageID?: string;\n  sessionID?: string;\n  text?: string;\n  tool?: string;\n  callID?: string;\n  state?: {\n    status?: string;\n    input?: unknown;\n    output?: unknown;\n    error?: unknown;\n    time?: { start?: number; end?: number };\n  };\n  time?: { start?: number; end?: number };\n}\n\ninterface OpencodeMessage {\n  info?: OpencodeMessageInfo;\n  parts?: OpencodePart[];\n}\n\nexport interface OpencodeExport {\n  info?: OpencodeSessionInfo;\n  messages?: OpencodeMessage[];\n}\n\n/** What `opencode session list --format json` returns, per row. */\ninterface OpencodeSessionRow {\n  id?: string;\n  title?: string;\n  directory?: string;\n  updated?: number;\n}\n\n/** One part, paired with the message that owns it and its session position. */\ninterface FlatPart {\n  info: OpencodeMessageInfo;\n  part: OpencodePart;\n  seq: number;\n}\n\nfunction packageVersion(): string {\n  try {\n    const pkg = JSON.parse(\n      readFileSync(new URL(\"../../package.json\", import.meta.url), \"utf8\"),\n    ) as { version?: string };\n    return pkg.version ?? \"0.1.0\";\n  } catch {\n    return \"0.1.0\";\n  }\n}\n\nfunction sanitizeId(id: string): string {\n  return id.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/g, \"_\");\n}\n\nfunction cursorPath(repo: RepoInfo, sessionId: string): string {\n  return join(repo.commonDir, \"conversation-ledger\", \"cursors\", `${sanitizeId(sessionId)}.json`);\n}\n\nasync function readCursor(repo: RepoInfo, sessionId: string): Promise<number> {\n  try {\n    const raw = await readFile(cursorPath(repo, sessionId), \"utf8\");\n    const data = JSON.parse(raw) as { parts?: number };\n    return typeof data.parts === \"number\" ? data.parts : 0;\n  } catch {\n    return 0;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function writeCursor(repo: RepoInfo, sessionId: string, parts: number): Promise<void> {\n  const path = cursorPath(repo, sessionId);\n  await mkdir(join(repo.commonDir, \"conversation-ledger\", \"cursors\"), { recursive: true });\n  await writeFile(path, JSON.stringify({ parts }) + \"\\n\");\n}\n\n/** opencode stores times as epoch milliseconds; the ledger wants ISO 8601. */\nfunction isoFromMs(ms: unknown): string | null {\n  if (typeof ms !== \"number\" || !Number.isFinite(ms)) return null;\n  const date = new Date(ms);\n  return Number.isNaN(date.getTime()) ? null : date.toISOString();\n}\n\n/**\n * Run an opencode subcommand and return its stdout.\n *\n * The child's stdout goes to a temp *file*, never a pipe. opencode (a Bun\n * binary) exits without draining a piped stdout, so anything past ~64KB is\n * silently lost — a large session's export still parses as JSON right up to\n * the truncation point in some cases, which would quietly capture a partial\n * conversation. Writing to a real file descriptor returns the full output.\n *\n * Returns null when opencode is not installed or the command fails; every\n * caller treats that as \"nothing to capture\" rather than an error, so a\n * missing opencode never breaks a hook.\n */\nasync function runOpencode(args: string[], cwd: string): Promise<string | null> {\n  const dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), \"cledger-opencode-\"));\n  const path = join(dir, \"out.json\");\n  try {\n    const handle = await open(path, \"w\");\n    try {\n      const code = await new Promise<number | null>((resolve, re