{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_013nJ1ckYMauSeTkhAYNMMzK","input":{"command":"cd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\" && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\n0.17.0: opencode adapter\n\nopencode is the first source without an append-only transcript file: sessions\nlive in a mutable SQLite database. Rather than read that database — whose\nschema is visibly mid-migration, and which also stores API tokens — capture\nshells out to `opencode export --pure <id>` and converts its JSON.\n\nEvents are one per *part*, not per message. opencode's store is mutable and a\nmessage accumulates parts over time, so a part is the finest unit that stops\nchanging; a message that gains parts after an early idle then appends rather\nthan re-emitting changed content under a new id. Tool calls that have not\nsettled are skipped and hold the cursor back until they finish.\n\nTwo differences from the existing adapters are deliberate. opencode's\n`reasoning` parts are plaintext, not provider-encrypted, so they convert to\nordinary visible `thinking` blocks instead of the opaque `reasoning` kind\nCodex needs. And opencode states the model on user messages as well as\nassistant ones, so `producer.model` is recorded there too — claude-code\nstates no model on a user line and none is invented.\n\n`cledger install opencode` writes a `session.idle` plugin to\n`~/.config/opencode/plugin/cledger.js`, which spawns the normal hook\nentrypoint detached so the TUI is never blocked or written over.\n\nWorked around upstream: `opencode export` exits without draining a piped\nstdout, truncating any session over ~64KB into JSON that can still parse.\nThe child now writes to a temp file instead.\n\nOnly `text`, `reasoning` and `tool` parts are claimed as convertible, and\nonly `step-start`/`step-finish`/`patch` as deliberately skipped. The `file`,\n`agent`, `snapshot` and `todo` types opencode's binary references are left\nunclassified on purpose, so they route through the drift path — preserved\nraw-only and upgradeable by `cledger renormalize` — rather than being\nsilently discarded on speculation.\n\nSubagent sessions are skipped, matching claude-code's sidechain handling.\nCapturing them properly is a cross-adapter schema question, now on the\nroadmap along with the positional-seq caveat this mutable store introduces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YZSeAzTwQ9ikr7D6aiZ8vq\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the opencode adapter"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","head":"5476c74237583d41f5acff542b07f3b2eb42daf0","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","seq":432},"id":"ev1-ff17176b30dd377641541700e6c33c7641c60056a85f721640f6a685a9ee525b","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-02T17:17:36.352Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_013nJ1ckYMauSeTkhAYNMMzK","input":{"command":"cd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\" && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\n0.17.0: opencode adapter\n\nopencode is the first source without an append-only transcript file: sessions\nlive in a mutable SQLite database. Rather than read that database — whose\nschema is visibly mid-migration, and which also stores API tokens — capture\nshell