{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01XDQKDWaYZppBR354KyPq3V","input":{"command":"cd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\" && gh pr create --draft --title \"0.17.0: opencode adapter\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdds `src/adapters/opencode.ts`, wired into `cledger hook`, `cledger capture`, `cledger install`, `renormalize`, and the public library surface.\n\n## Why it looks different from the other two\n\nopencode is the first source with no append-only transcript file — sessions live in a mutable SQLite DB at `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. Rather than read that DB, capture shells out to `opencode export --pure <id>`:\n\n- cledger has zero runtime deps and supports Node >= 20; `node:sqlite` would force both to change.\n- The schema is visibly mid-migration (an empty `session_message` table sits beside the populated `message`/`part` tables it evidently replaces).\n- That same DB holds `credential.value` and `account.access_token`. Reading conversations shouldn't mean opening the file that stores API tokens.\n\n`--sanitize` is deliberately not passed — cledger does its own redaction, and letting opencode rewrite content would make event ids depend on opencode's version.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**One event per part, not per message.** The store is mutable and a message accumulates parts over time. A part is the finest unit that stops changing, so a message that gains parts after an early `session.idle` appends rather than re-emitting changed content under a new id. Unsettled (`running`) tool calls are skipped *and* hold the cursor back, so they're captured once they finish rather than skipped forever.\n\n**Reasoning is visible, not opaque.** opencode stores reasoning as plain text, unlike Codex's provider-encrypted `encrypted_content`. So it becomes an ordinary `thinking` block in a `conversation_turn` — no opacity marker, nothing withheld.\n\n**Model recorded on user messages too.** opencode states the model on user messages; claude-code doesn't, and there none is invented. Here the source states it, so it's recorded.\n\n**Conservative type classification.** Only `text`/`reasoning`/`tool` are claimed convertible and only `step-start`/`step-finish`/`patch` deliberately skipped. The `file`, `agent`, `snapshot` and `todo` types opencode's binary references are left unclassified on purpose — they route through the drift path (preserved raw-only, warned about, upgradeable by `cledger renormalize`) instead of being discarded on speculation.\n\n**Subagent sessions skipped**, matching claude-code's sidechain handling. Doing it properly is a cross-adapter schema question, now on the roadmap.\n\n## Upstream bug worked around\n\n`opencode export` exits without draining a piped stdout, silently truncating at ~64KB — and the truncated JSON can still parse, so this would have quietly captured partial conversations. The child now writes to a temp file. Verified: 65516 bytes over a pipe vs 446703 to a file descriptor.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 170 tests pass (169 + 1 pre-existing skip), including 5 new adapter tests covering conversion, drift preservation, `occurred_at` fallbacks, idempotent re-capture, unsettled-tool cursor hold, subagent skip, and tool errors.\n- End-to-end against a real 378KB opencode session: 18 events, matching the source part histogram exactly (11 tool, 5 reasoning, 2 text), re-capture appends 0.\n- The generated plugin loads inside real opencode with no errors; install is idempotent.\n\n## Known gaps (on the roadmap)\n\n- `conversation.seq` is positional over a mutable store, so a `session revert` can shift positions and duplicate the parts after the deletion. Per-part capture keeps the blast radius small.\n- The plugin reads `session.idle`'s session id defensively across several key names — opencode's `Event` union isn't in the installed SDK typings and a live event capture couldn't be completed. Falls back to the most recently updated session for the directory.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YZSeAzTwQ9ikr7D6aiZ8vq\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open draft PR"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","head":"5476c74237583d41f5acff542b07f3b2eb42daf0","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","seq":437},"id":"ev1-acfb3c0ea7cb50c988904a6335b5c8728330cfc2a3695ad0b241e192ba773f68","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-02T17:18:06.106Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01XDQKDWaYZppBR354KyPq3V","input":{"command":"cd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\" && gh pr create --draft --title \"0.17.0: opencode adapter\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdds `src/adapters/opencode.ts`, wired into `cledger hook`, `cledger capture`, `cledger install`, `renormalize`, and the public library surface.\n\n## Why it looks different from the other two\n\nopencode is the first source with no append-only transcript file — sessions live in a mutable SQLite DB at `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. Rather than read that DB, capture shells out to `opencode export --pure <id>`:\n\n- cledger has zero runtime deps and supports Node >= 20; `node:sqlite` would force both to change.\n- The schema is visibly mid-migration (an empty `session_message` table sits beside the populated `message`/`part` tabl