{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"I've finished the investigation. Here's what I found and where I need your call.\n\n## What opencode actually stores (v1.18.5, installed locally)\n\nNot JSONL files like the other two adapters — **SQLite** at `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. Tables: `session`, `message`, `part` (plus an empty `session_message` that looks like an in-flight schema migration — evidence the DB shape is still moving).\n\nBut there's a much better door: **`opencode export <sessionID>`** emits clean JSON on stdout in 0.36s — `{info, messages: [{info, parts: [...]}]}` with stable ids on every session/message/part. `opencode session list --format json` enumerates sessions **scoped to the cwd's project**, which is exactly the repo-scoped discovery a backfill needs. `--pure` (skip external plugins) produced byte-identical output.\n\nContent model: a **message** has `role`, `modelID`, `providerID`, `agent`/`mode`, `time.created/completed`. Its **parts** are `text`, `reasoning`, `tool`, `step-start`, `step-finish`, `patch` (and the binary also references `file`, `agent`, `snapshot`, `todo` part types I didn't see in my data). A `tool` part carries call input *and* output in one object.\n\nThree findings that matter:\n\n1. **`reasoning` parts are plaintext**, not provider-encrypted. Nothing like Codex's `encrypted_content`. So they map to visible `thinking` blocks, not the opaque `reasoning` kind.\n2. **The store is mutable.** `session.revert`, `message.removed`, `part.removed` all exist, and `opencode session delete` is a CLI command. Every existing adapter relies on an append-only file where line index is a stable `conversation.seq`. That assumption does not hold here — a revert can shift positions and churn event ids.\n3. An assistant *message* spans multiple LLM round-trips (I saw 5 `step-start`s across 4 assistant messages), so a \"message\" ≈ a whole agent turn, not one API call.\n\nTrigger story: opencode has a plugin API (`Hooks.event`) and the binary emits a **`session.idle`** bus event — the natural `Stop`-hook equivalent. `cledger install opencode` would drop a JS plugin in `~/.config/opencode/plugin/`.\n\nTwo hazards worth flagging now: the DB also holds `credential.value` and `account.access_token`, so direct SQLite reads have a much larger blast radius than the export CLI; and your `~/.config/opencode/` has **both** `opencode.json` and `opencode.jsonc`, which would make a config-editing installer ambiguous (the plugin *directory* avoids touching config at all).\n\nAlso: `opencode export --sanitize` exists. I'd deliberately not use it — cledger has its own redaction stack, and letting opencode rewrite content would make event ids depend on opencode's version.\n\nNow the decisions I can't make for you:","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","head":"5476c74237583d41f5acff542b07f3b2eb42daf0","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","seq":179},"id":"ev1-c9f0845a2104c9fd4b8e8d5ba87a205cf23f75c295dba705ae203f7c06a6c3ab","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-02T16:51:52.121Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"I've finished the investigation. Here's what I found and where I need your call.\n\n## What opencode actually stores (v1.18.5, installed locally)\n\nNot JSONL files like the other two adapters — **SQLite** at `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. Tables: `session`, `message`, `part` (plus an empty `