{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Investigation and implementation are both done. Sanity checks run: full suite (170 tests, 169 pass, 1 pre-existing skip), an end-to-end capture of a real 378KB opencode session (18 events, matching the source part histogram exactly, re-capture appends 0), the generated plugin loading inside real opencode with no errors, and a clean working tree.\n\n**What shipped** — `src/adapters/opencode.ts` plus wiring into `cledger hook`, `cledger capture`, `cledger install`, `renormalize`, and the library exports, on PR #2 (draft): https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/2\n\nAll four of your answers are implemented as chosen. The things worth your attention:\n\n**An upstream bug I nearly shipped past.** `opencode export` exits without draining a piped stdout, cutting off at ~64KB — and the truncated JSON still parses. A pipe-based adapter would have silently captured partial conversations with no error. The child now writes to a temp file instead (65516 bytes piped vs 446703 to a file descriptor). Worth reporting to opencode; the workaround should stay regardless.\n\n**Two claims in my earlier report I had to revise while building.** The `session.idle` payload shape is not something I could pin down — the live probe hung on the ds4 model call, and opencode's `Event` union isn't in the installed SDK typings. So the plugin reads the session id across several plausible keys and the hook treats it as optional, falling back to the most-recently-updated session for the directory. And I'd planned to inherit stderr from the spawned child; that would have written into opencode's TUI while it draws, so it's discarded — meaning drift warnings only surface on a manual `cledger capture opencode --all`. Both are on the roadmap with what would close them.\n\n**Deliberately left conservative**: only `text`/`reasoning`/`tool` are claimed convertible and only `step-start`/`step-finish`/`patch` skipped. The `file`, `agent`, `snapshot`, `todo` types opencode's binary references are unclassified on purpose so they hit the drift path — preserved raw-only and upgradeable by `renormalize` — rather than being discarded on a guess. The real session I tested produced zero unrecognized parts, so those types are untested against live data.\n\nYour subagent TODO is on the roadmap as a cross-adapter item covering claude-code, codex and opencode together, framed around the schema question that blocks all three (a `spawned_by` link or `conversation.parent`, plus how `cledger log` should display nested turns) rather than as per-adapter plumbing. The mutable-store `seq` caveat is documented there too.\n\nresult: opencode adapter shipped in cledger 0.17.0 as draft PR #2 — reads via `opencode export` rather than SQLite, one event per part, `session.idle` plugin trigger; found and worked around an upstream 64KB piped-stdout truncation bug that would have silently captured partial conversations.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","head":"5476c74237583d41f5acff542b07f3b2eb42daf0","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","seq":456},"id":"ev1-dadf568aeb3259dbd3b4a7de656ccbe125a14671cef04348461f7dacf8028aa3","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-02T17:18:56.969Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"fe9cea6b-80c2-4e6e-bff4-aa88447380f6","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/opencode-adapter","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-opencode-adapter","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Investigation and implementation are both done. Sanity checks run: full suite (170 tests, 169 pass, 1 pre-existing skip), an end-to-end capture of a real 378KB opencode session (18 events, matching the source part histogram exactly, re-capture appends 0), the generated plugin loading inside real opencode with no errors, and a clean working tree.\n\n**What shipped** — `src/adapters/opencode.ts` plus wiring into `cledger hook`, `cledger capture`, `cledger install`, `renormalize`, and the library exports, on PR #2 (draft): https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/2\n\nAll four of your answers are implemented as chosen. The things worth your attention:\n\n**An upstream bug I nearly shipped past.** `opencode export` exits without draining a piped stdout, cutting off at ~64KB — and the truncated JSON still parses. A pipe-based adapter would have silently captured partial conversations with no error. The child now writes to a temp file instead (65516 bytes piped vs 446703 to a file descriptor). Worth reporting to opencode; the workaround should stay regardless.\n\n**Two claims in my earlier report I had to revise while building.** The `session.idle` payload shape is not something I could pin down — the live probe hung on the ds4 model call, and opencode's `Event` union isn't in the installed SDK typings. So the plugin reads the session id across several plausible keys and the hook treats it as optional, falling back to the most-recently-updated session for the directory. And I'd planned to inherit stderr from the spawned child; that would have written into opencode's TUI while it draws, so it's discarded — meaning drift warnings only surface on a manual `cledger capture opencode --all`. Both are on the roadmap with what would close them.\n\n**Deliberately left conservative**: only `text`/`reasoning`/`tool` are claimed convertible and only `step-start`/`step-finish`/`patch` skipped. The `file`, `agent`, `snapshot`, `todo` types opencode's binary references are unclassified on purpose so they hit the drift path — preserved raw-